Clypra — https://github.com/AIEraDev/Clypra
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Adapted in the following SundaySync files:

  crates/core/src/peaks.rs
      The per-bucket waveform statistic — absolute peak paired with root-mean-
      square energy, carried together rather than either alone — is adapted from
      Clypra's `compute_waveform_buckets` in `src-tauri/src/commands/media.rs`.
      SundaySync's version streams a multi-resolution pyramid out of the existing
      analysis cache rather than computing a single fixed bucket count over a
      fully-resident sample buffer; the statistic per bucket is the shared part.
      See docs/DECISIONS.md D-052 and D-053.

  app/src/timeline/waveformDraw.ts
      The draw loop's structure — one pass over pre-computed buckets, drawing a
      peak outline behind an RMS body — is adapted from Clypra's
      `drawProfessionalWaveform` in `src/lib/utils/canvasUtils.ts`. SundaySync's
      version draws both bars symmetric around the clip's vertical centre (peak
      AND RMS, rather than RMS substituting for peak) and gets its bucket
      positions from the on-disk pyramid (`peaks.rs`, above) intersected against
      the visible viewport, rather than a buffer resampled to a fixed count; the
      one-pass-over-buckets shape is the shared part. See docs/DECISIONS.md
      D-053 ("planned (S4)").

